CORE
main.ii
--winx64 --cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ default calling convention: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Two partial specializations that differ only in a calling convention,
which cbmc ignores, have the same symbol.  The second replaced the first's
declaration but kept the first's template scope, so its parameters R and A
were unbound and the specialization never matched.  The MSVC STL's
std::function is based on _Get_function_impl<_Ret __cdecl(_Types...)> and
<_Ret __vectorcall(_Types...)>.
